                "apprentice": "The true sight deepens, revealing hidden magical effects, disguised opponents, and concealed weapons during melee. The Knight can see through illusions that would mislead lesser fighters, ensuring their blade always strikes true. The technique makes deceptive fighting styles useless against the Knight.\n\nThe enhancement to blade capability transforms the blade-fighter's approach to hand-to-hand range. What begins as a significant advantage in isolated strikes becomes a systemic shift across the entire engagement.",
                "adept": "Professional-grade true sight for melee operations. The Knight sees through all illusions and deceptions in close quarters, perceiving opponents' true forms and positions regardless of magical concealment. The Knight cannot be fooled by combat tricks, illusions, or disguised threats — their blade always finds the real target.\n\nA close-quarters specialist with this enhancement operates at a decisive advantage in close-range capability. The Knight fights on ground they have shaped — stone walls channel opponents toward the blade, spikes create kill zones, and the ground itself becomes a weapon.",
                "expert": "The Knight's true sight approaches the practical ceiling of melee perception. No illusion, disguise, or magical concealment can deceive the Knight in close quarters. The Knight sees the battlefield as it truly is, making deceptive fighting styles completely useless and ensuring their blade always connects with reality.\n\nA close-quarters specialist with this enhancement reads an entire melee at once, tracking the committed intent of several concealed attackers rather than a single foe. The Knight anticipates coordinated feints a fraction of a second before they land, redirecting multiple blades into the kill zones they have shaped.",
                "master": "At this level, true sight is the Knight's blade made manifest — combat and spell are indistinguishable. The Knight perceives the unvarnished truth of the melee environment — no illusion, disguise, or concealment can deceive them. The Knight is a truth-seer in close quarters — their blade strikes only what is real, and no magical deception can protect opponents from the Knight's penetrating gaze.\n\nFrom a tactical perspective, the peak improvement in close-range capability is clear and measurable. The close-quarters specialist who masters this enhancement dictates the melee."
