            "oneiric_interface": {
                "beginner": "The Knight can enter a combat trance — a waking dream state where blade-work flows from instinct rather than conscious thought. The dream walking provides basic combat flow, allowing the Knight to react without the delay of conscious decision-making during melee.\n\nThe enhancement to melee capability transforms the fighter's approach to hand-to-hand range. What begins as a noticeable advantage in isolated strikes becomes a systemic shift across the entire engagement.",
                "apprentice": "The combat trance deepens, allowing the Knight to fight in a state of perfect blade-dream. The Knight's body moves with the fluid certainty of a dreamer — every technique is available without conscious selection, and the blade finds its mark through instinctive rather than deliberate action. The dream state makes the Knight's fighting style unpredictable.\n\nThe considerable enhancement to close-range capability The Knight uses the edge to turn a risky parry into a winning riposte when an opponent's blade is a hair's breadth from landing.",
                "adept": "Professional-grade combat dreaming for melee operations. The Knight fights in a state of perfect blade-dream where conscious thought and physical action merge. The Knight doesn't plan their techniques — they dream them, and the blade follows. The dream state makes the Knight's fighting style remarkably creative and extraordinarily difficult to predict.\n\nThe returns from blade capability scale progressively through sustained close-quarters fighting. An early decisive edge widens as the engagement continues, and the blade-fighter who endures longest dominates most completely.",
                "expert": "The Knight's combat dreaming approaches the practical ceiling of melee instinctive fighting. The Knight fights in a state where blade and dream are one — techniques manifest as dreamt, parries arise from instinct, and the Knight fights with the creative freedom of a lucid dreamer. Opponents cannot predict the Knight's blade because the Knight themselves doesn't consciously choose their techniques.\n\nThe melee capability this provides changes the fundamental rhythm of blade-work. Each blow flows more efficiently, and the cumulative effect across a full engagement is dramatic.",
                "master": "The Knight who has fully mastered combat dreaming fights at the height of close-quarters capability. The Knight fights in a state of perfect blade-dream where every technique is available instantly and executed with near-perfect instinctive precision. The Knight doesn't think about blade-work — they dream it, and their blade makes the dream real. This is the highest form of melee combat: action without thought, blade without hesitation, victory without doubt.\n\nThis improvement to melee capability adds tactical depth to every strike within the clinch. The fighter gains options that unenhanced practitioners simply do not have, and each additional option represents a extraordinary expansion of their combat repertoire."
            },
