                "expert": "The Knight's causal control approaches the practical ceiling of melee causality manipulation. The Knight can ensure that their strikes always precede the opponent's defenses in the causal chain, making their attacks effectively inevitable. The technique makes the Knight's blade the first and final word in any melee exchange — cause and effect bend toward the Knight's strikes.\n\nThe returns from cause-before-effect strikes where the wound appears before the blade connects scale progressively through sustained close-quarters fighting. An early decisive edge widens as the engagement continues, and the fighter who endures longest presses most completely.",
                "master": "In the Knight's hands, causality manipulation reaches the pinnacle of close-quarters application. The Knight influences the causal chain of melee with devastating effectiveness, ensuring their strikes always precede the opponent's defenses. The Knight's blade is the first cause in any melee exchange — the opponent can only react to a strike that has already been destined to connect.\n\nThe peak improvement in cause-before-effect strikes where the wound appears before the blade connects reshapes how the fighter approaches the melee. Each clash demonstrates the combatant establishes edge that accumulates across each support cycle blows."
