                "adept": "Professional-grade mana transfer for artillery operations. The Bombardment mage can efficiently transfer mana between themselves and allies, or sacrifice personal reserves to fuel enhanced bombardment. The Reactor Transfer provides emergency options when conventional mana management fails — the Bombardment mage can always fire a few more rounds by paying a personal price.\n\nThis improvement to mana-channeling that keeps artillery firing when reserves would normally deplete adds tactical depth to every salvo within the bombardment exchange. The artillery mage gains options that unenhanced practitioners simply do not have, and each additional option represents a clear expansion of their combat repertoire.",
                "expert": "The Bombardment mage's Reactor Transfer approaches the practical ceiling of combat mana transfer. The mage can efficiently sacrifice personal mana to fuel devastating enhanced bombardment or replenish critically depleted allies. The sacrifice ensures the Bombardment mage always has one more salvo left, even when conventional mana management says they should be empty.\n\nThe overwhelming improvement in mana-channeling that keeps artillery firing when reserves would normally deplete reshapes how the fire-support approaches ranged combat. Each volley demonstrates the bombardment platform establishes fire-superiority that accumulates across each support cycle engagements.",
                "master": "Reactor Transfer operates at the highest practical level of bombardment augmentation. The Bombardment mage can sacrifice personal mana with devastating efficiency to fuel enhanced bombardment or replenish allies. The mage is a warrior who always has one more salvo — their willingness to sacrifice ensures the fire never stops, the ally never falls, and the bombardment never ends while the Bombardment mage still draws breath.\n\nThe paramount gains in bombardment capability create building advantage that compounds rapidly. Each successful bombardment in long-range fighting makes the next one easier, and the bombardment platform who seizes the initiative early suppresses the engagement from that point forward."
